From: Neutron
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: a composition swap chain's Present completes without a Vulkan surface

Mister Horse Product Manager 3.7.7 (JUCE 8; the app Animation Composer is installed with) drew its first frame and
never another: buttons did not hover, Next did not leave the Welcome screen, a maximized window kept the old frame.
JUCE 8 draws through a swap chain from CreateSwapChainForComposition with DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_FRAME_LATENCY_
WAITABLE_OBJECT (FLIP_SEQUENTIAL, 2 buffers) and waits on the waitable object before every paint.

DXVK gives a composition swap chain (no window) its own hidden dummy window and presents to a Vulkan swap chain on
it. A FIFO frame's completion is a present-wait on that surface, and a window that is never shown never shows the
frame: the presenter's frame thread called vkWaitForPresentKHR(presentId 17, 100 ms) 250 times in 30 s for the one
frame JUCE presented, so the frame latency fence was never signaled and the semaphore behind the waitable object
(initial count 1) was never released (WINEDEBUG=+sync: 0 NtReleaseSemaphore all session). The app's second wait
never returned.

On Windows a composition swap chain's Present hands the buffer to the compositor; Present completes, the frame is
counted and the waitable object is released once per presented frame, paced by DWM. Here the compositor's side is
Wine's dcomp bridge, which reads the presented buffer back (GetBuffer) and copies it to the visual's window. So a
swap chain whose surface factory owns DXVK's dummy window (DXVKDUMMYWNDCLASS: CreateSwapChainForComposition is the
one way to get one) now has no Vulkan presenter at all, as the GDI-present chains already have none: Present flushes,
rotates the buffers as before, counts the frame and signals the latency fence, so the waitable object is released
per frame. SyncInterval > 0 is paced to the display's refresh (EnumDisplaySettings), sleeping outside the immediate
context lock, never spinning. The bridge's fallback window for an unmatched Present stays the dummy window
(dcomp_set_pending_hwnd, which DxgiSurfaceFactory::CreateSurface called for the presenter that is no longer made).
Color spaces other than sRGB are reported unsupported for such chains (there is no surface to ask). Logged once per
chain: "neutron-comp-present".

Not covered: D3D12 composition swap chains (vkd3d-proton's own swap chain); the pacing uses the primary display's
refresh, not the monitor the visual is on.

Lab, 11.10-183m (183rc + this + dxvk-dxgi 0005), NVIDIA 615.78, Wayland. Product Manager, Welcome -> hover -> Next:
fix 2/2 (f1, kf2): hover repaints the button (present 2 -> 3), Next shows the sign-in screen (window luma 238 -> 36,
presents 5), and 2/2 sign-in runs drew and showed the app's dialog after a link (g1, g2).
NEUTRON_DXVK_COMPOSITION_PRESENT=0 on the same build: 1 present all session and Next changes nothing, 2/2 (kA1, kA2).
Other programs, all composition swap chains enabled (CLI change of the same day), n=1 each, all draw: FL Studio 2026
(WebView2 chain 639x1858: its GPU process 39.1% / 47.6% of a core vs 67.2% with the kill switch; all processes
97 / 113% vs 107%), Ableton Live 12 (one composition chain, 19.3% total), CapCut, Topaz Photo, Affinity, Cavalry
(no composition chain: unaffected).
Adobe (the Adobe confs give every exe composition chains), this build vs 183rc's DXVK on the same prefix copy, n=1
each: Photoshop 2026 Home (WebView2, 2 composition chains through this path) and a recent document draw the same;
blits 15 vs 14, 0 'Invalid buffer ID', 9.9% vs 9.9% of a core. Premiere 2026 Home + the Waterfalls project
(program monitor, timeline, thumbnails) draw the same; blits 21 vs 22, 0 'Invalid buffer ID', 11.2% vs 20.4%.

Kill switch NEUTRON_DXVK_COMPOSITION_PRESENT=0 (the Vulkan presenter on the dummy window).

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
index aecf5275..cd668ba9 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
       m_gdiPresent = env::getEnvVar("NEUTRON_GDI_PRESENT") == "1";
     }
 
+    InitCompositionPresent();
+
     if (m_gdiPresent) {
       HWND hwnd = static_cast<DxgiSurfaceFactory*>(m_surfaceFactory.ptr())->GetWindow();
       Logger::warn(str::format("neutron-gdi-present: hwnd=", (void*)hwnd,
@@ -306,8 +308,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
       if (hr != S_OK)
         return hr;
 
-      if (m_gdiPresent)
-        return S_OK; /* neutron N2: GDI path is never occluded-blocked */
+      if (m_gdiPresent || m_compPresent)
+        return S_OK; /* neutron N2: GDI path is never occluded-blocked; nor is a composition chain */
       VkResult status = m_presenter->checkSwapChainStatus();
       return status == VK_SUCCESS ? S_OK : DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED;
     }
@@ -326,6 +328,13 @@ namespace dxvk {
       hr = E_FAIL;
     }
 
+    // NEUTRON composition present: the frame is complete once its buffers rotated. Pace it outside the
+    // immediate context lock, then signal it (SyncFrameLatency below releases the waitable object).
+    if (m_compPresent && hr == S_OK) {
+      PaceCompositionPresent(SyncInterval);
+      m_frameLatencySignal->signal(m_frameId);
+    }
+
     // Ensure to synchronize and release the frame latency semaphore
     // even if presentation failed with STATUS_OCCLUDED, or otherwise
     // applications using the semaphore may deadlock. This works because
@@ -353,7 +362,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     VkColorSpaceKHR vkColorSpace = ConvertColorSpace(ColorSpace);
 
-    if (m_gdiPresent) /* neutron N2: sRGB only */
+    if (m_gdiPresent || m_compPresent) /* neutron N2: sRGB only (composition: no surface to ask) */
       return (vkColorSpace == VK_COLOR_SPACE_SRGB_NONLINEAR_KHR)
         ? DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_COLOR_SPACE_SUPPORT_FLAG_PRESENT : 0;
 
@@ -368,7 +377,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
           DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_TYPE     ColorSpace) {
     VkColorSpaceKHR colorSpace = ConvertColorSpace(ColorSpace);
 
-    if (m_gdiPresent) { /* neutron N2 */
+    if (m_gdiPresent || m_compPresent) { /* neutron N2 */
       if (colorSpace != VK_COLOR_SPACE_SRGB_NONLINEAR_KHR)
         return E_INVALIDARG;
       m_colorSpace = colorSpace;
@@ -784,6 +793,16 @@ namespace dxvk {
     if (m_gdiPresent)
       return PresentImageGdi();
 
+    // NEUTRON composition present: no Vulkan swap chain; the dcomp bridge reads back the presented buffer.
+    if (m_compPresent) {
+      if (m_backBuffers.size() > 1u)
+        RotateBackBuffers(immediateContext);
+
+      immediateContext->FlushCsChunk();
+      m_frameId += 1;
+      return S_OK;
+    }
+
     m_presenter->setSyncInterval(SyncInterval);
 
     // Presentation semaphores and WSI swap chain image
@@ -874,6 +893,75 @@ namespace dxvk {
   }
 
 
+  void D3D11SwapChain::InitCompositionPresent() {
+    // CreateSwapChainForComposition is the one way to a DxgiSurfaceFactory without an app window: it then
+    // owns DXVK's dummy window. The bit-blt GDI path stays as it was (NEUTRON_GDI_PRESENT=1).
+    static const bool enabled = env::getEnvVar("NEUTRON_DXVK_COMPOSITION_PRESENT") != "0";
+
+    HWND hwnd = static_cast<DxgiSurfaceFactory*>(m_surfaceFactory.ptr())->GetWindow();
+    wchar_t cls[32] = { };
+
+    if (!enabled || m_gdiPresent || !hwnd || !::GetClassNameW(hwnd, cls, 32) || wcscmp(cls, L"DXVKDUMMYWNDCLASS"))
+      return;
+
+    m_compPresent = true;
+
+    DEVMODEW mode = { };
+    mode.dmSize = sizeof(mode);
+    uint32_t hz = ::EnumDisplaySettingsW(nullptr, ENUM_CURRENT_SETTINGS, &mode) && mode.dmDisplayFrequency > 1u
+      ? uint32_t(mode.dmDisplayFrequency) : 60u;
+    m_compRefreshPeriod = std::chrono::duration_cast<dxvk::high_resolution_clock::duration>(
+      std::chrono::nanoseconds(1000000000ull / hz));
+
+    // The dcomp bridge's fallback window for a Present it cannot match to a visual is the one DXVK last made a
+    // surface for (DxgiSurfaceFactory::CreateSurface), for a composition chain the dummy window. No surface is
+    // made now, so record it here as before.
+    using DcompSetPendingProc = void (*)(HWND);
+    HMODULE dcomp = ::GetModuleHandleA("dcomp.dll");
+
+    if (dcomp) {
+      auto setPending = reinterpret_cast<DcompSetPendingProc>(
+        reinterpret_cast<void*>(::GetProcAddress(dcomp, "dcomp_set_pending_hwnd")));
+
+      if (setPending)
+        setPending(hwnd);
+    }
+
+    Logger::info(str::format("neutron-comp-present: composition swap chain ", m_desc.Width, "x", m_desc.Height,
+      " effect=", m_desc.SwapEffect, " buffers=", m_desc.BufferCount, " flags=", m_desc.Flags,
+      ": presents complete without a Vulkan surface, paced at ", hz, " Hz"));
+  }
+
+
+  void D3D11SwapChain::PaceCompositionPresent(UINT SyncInterval) {
+    auto now = dxvk::high_resolution_clock::now();
+
+    if (SyncInterval) {
+      auto interval = m_compRefreshPeriod * SyncInterval;
+      auto due = m_compLastPresent + interval;
+
+      // Sleep, never spin: DWM's pacing costs the app no CPU on Windows.
+      if (due > now && due - now <= interval) {
+        using NtDelayExecutionProc = LONG (WINAPI*)(BOOLEAN, PLARGE_INTEGER);
+        static auto delay = reinterpret_cast<NtDelayExecutionProc>(reinterpret_cast<void*>(
+          ::GetProcAddress(::GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll"), "NtDelayExecution")));
+
+        LARGE_INTEGER ticks;
+        ticks.QuadPart = -std::max<int64_t>(1, std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(due - now).count() / 100);
+
+        if (delay)
+          delay(FALSE, &ticks);
+        else
+          ::Sleep(DWORD(std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(due - now).count()));
+
+        now = due;
+      }
+    }
+
+    m_compLastPresent = now;
+  }
+
+
   void D3D11SwapChain::RotateBackBuffers(D3D11ImmediateContext* ctx) {
     small_vector<Rc<DxvkImage>, 4> images;
 
@@ -985,8 +1073,8 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
   void D3D11SwapChain::CreatePresenter() {
     // neutron round-38 N2: GDI-present chains have NO Vulkan presenter at all
-    // (no vk swapchain, no wayland subsurface, no latency tracker).
-    if (m_gdiPresent)
+    // (no vk swapchain, no wayland subsurface, no latency tracker). Nor do composition chains.
+    if (m_gdiPresent || m_compPresent)
       return;
 
     PresenterDesc presenterDesc = { };
diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.h b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.h
index 5b25ee6a..30da77a6 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.h
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.h
@@ -133,6 +133,22 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     HRESULT PresentImageGdi();
 
+    // NEUTRON composition present: a swap chain made by CreateSwapChainForComposition has no window. DXVK
+    // gives it a hidden dummy window, and a Vulkan swap chain on that window never shows a frame, so a FIFO
+    // frame's present-wait never completed and the frame latency fence (and the app's waitable object) was
+    // never signaled after the first frame: JUCE 8 (Mister Horse Product Manager) waits on it before every
+    // paint and drew one frame. On Windows a composition chain's buffers go to the compositor, which Present
+    // hands them to; here the dcomp bridge reads the presented buffer back (GetBuffer). So such a chain has no
+    // presenter: Present completes (buffers rotate, the frame is signaled), paced to the display's refresh when
+    // SyncInterval > 0 as DWM paces it. Kill switch NEUTRON_DXVK_COMPOSITION_PRESENT=0.
+    bool m_compPresent = false;
+    dxvk::high_resolution_clock::time_point m_compLastPresent = { };
+    dxvk::high_resolution_clock::duration   m_compRefreshPeriod = { };
+
+    void InitCompositionPresent();
+
+    void PaceCompositionPresent(UINT SyncInterval);
+
     DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_DESC1     m_desc;
 
     Rc<DxvkDevice>            m_device;
